// A write through a pointer overwrites the location it points at.
//
// MoRDor's own test. Thread 2 reads back the address of G that thread 1
// published through A, writes 7 through it, and then reads G. In RC11 that read
// happens after the write through the pointer, which lands on G, so it cannot
// see G's initial 0.
//
// Coherence grouped writes by location without the execution's predicates, so
// `*rp := 7`, whose location is the symbol read from A, never shared a location
// with `G := 0`. co never ordered the two, and the read of the overwritten 0
// was coherent.
G := 0;
{
  rq := &G;
  A := rq
} ||| {
  rp := A;
  *rp := 7;
  r1 := G
}
%%
forbid (r1 = 0) [RC11]
